Algorithm
Step 1: Start.
Step 2: Declare an infix array, a postfix array, and a stack. Step 3: Initialize top = -1 and postfix index j = 0.
Step 4: Read the infix expression from the user.
Step 5: Scan the infix expression from left to right, one character at a time, until the null character '\0' is reached.
Step 6: If the current character is an operand (letter or digit), append it directly to the postfix expression.
Step 7: If the current character is an opening parenthesis (, push it onto the stack.
Step 8: If the current character is a closing parenthesis ):
•	a. Pop operators from the stack and append them to postfix until ( is found or the stack becomes empty.
•	b. If ( is found, pop it and do not append it to postfix. Step 9: If the current character is an operator:
•	a. While the stack is not empty and the top is not (: o	If the top operator has higher precedence than the current operator, 
pop it to postfix. o	If both have equal precedence and the current operator is not ^, pop the top operator to postfix.
o	Otherwise, stop popping.
•	b. Push the current operator onto the stack.
 
Step 10: After all input characters are processed, pop all remaining stack operators and append them to postfix.
Step 11: Add '\0' at the end of the postfix array. Step 12: Display the postfix expression.
Step 13: Stop.


